Subject: [PATCH 1/3] sidebar: expand-on-hover easing from a pref

Why Firefox source must change:
  The launcher animation hard-codes easing "ease-in-out". Aequera's motion
  token is the swift curve cubic-bezier(0.3,0.7,0.3,1); prefs/CSS cannot
  reach a WAAPI option set in JS.

What it changes:
  - New pref sidebar.animation.expand-on-hover.easing (lazy getter; default
    "ease-in-out", so Firefox behavior is unchanged when unset).
  - Applies to the expand-on-hover animation only.
  - An unparseable value falls back to the default with a console error
    instead of throwing from element.animate() (config failure must recover).

Depends on: nothing.
Validation: aequera/shell/firefox/tests/browser (easing + invalid-easing
  fallback); upstream browser_sidebar_animation.js stays green under Firefox
  defaults.
Upstream risk: low-medium; touches the options block of
  _animateSidebarContainer.

